# City Intel Pipeline (CIP) — Technical Specification v1.0
**ConectandoEnsenada Internal System**  
**Documento de Trabajo**  
**Fecha:** 28 Julio 2026  
**Estado:** Diseño listo para implementación

---

## 1. Mission

Turn any public business reference into a structured, verified, approval-ready draft listing with minimal human effort.

The human becomes the **editor**, not the data-entry operator.

---

## 2. Core Principles

- Never invent facts
- Prefer official and authoritative sources
- Always record every source used
- Flag all uncertainty clearly
- Use placeholders instead of fabricated assets
- Every step must be modular (easy to improve or replace later)
- Output must be ready for human approval in one glance

---

## 3. Supported Inputs (Trigger)

The pipeline accepts one or more of the following:

| Input Type          | Example                              | Priority |
|---------------------|--------------------------------------|----------|
| TikTok URL          | Link to video or profile             | High     |
| Instagram profile   | @business or post link               | High     |
| Facebook page       | Page URL                             | High     |
| Google Maps link    | Place link or share link             | Very High|
| Website             | Official domain                      | Very High|
| YouTube video       | Video or channel                     | Medium   |
| PDF                 | Menu, brochure, flyer                | Medium   |
| Image               | Photo of storefront, card, menu      | Medium   |
| Business card       | Photo or scan                        | Medium   |
| Plain text          | Just the business name + city        | Low      |

Multiple inputs can be given at the same time for better results.

---

## 4. High-Level Workflow
Input(s)
↓

Identify Business
↓
Collect Public Information
↓
Build Unified Profile
↓
Detect Duplicates
↓
Analyze Completeness & Quality
↓
Generate SEO + Tags + Embeddings
↓
Handle Assets (photos, logo, etc.)
↓
Calculate Confidence Score
↓
Produce Approval Package
↓
Wait for Human Decision
├── Approve → Publish
├── Edit → Re-process
└── Reject → Archive with reason

text---

## 5. Detailed Stages

### Stage 1 — Identify Business
- Extract name, possible address, phone, category
- Normalize name (remove “S.A. de C.V.”, extra words, etc.)
- Generate possible search variations

### Stage 2 — Collect Public Information
Sources in order of preference:
1. Official website
2. Google Maps / Google Business Profile
3. Government registries (when available)
4. Facebook / Instagram official pages
5. Other public directories
6. Social proof (reviews, mentions)

Every piece of data must store:
- Value
- Source URL
- Confidence (high / medium / low)
- Date collected

### Stage 3 — Build Unified Profile
Create a clean internal object that matches the `places` + `business_details` schema used in ConectandoEnsenada.

### Stage 4 — Duplicate Detection
- Compare against existing `places` table
- Use name similarity + location proximity + phone/website matching
- Return possible matches with score

### Stage 5 — Completeness Analysis
Check against required and nice-to-have fields:

**Critical**
- Name
- Category
- Location (at least neighborhood or coordinates)
- At least one contact method

**Important**
- Phone / WhatsApp
- Address
- Opening hours
- Description
- Photos

**Nice to have**
- Website
- Social links
- Price range
- Amenities
- Menu

### Stage 6 — SEO & Enrichment
- Generate slug
- SEO title + description (ES + EN)
- Suggest categories and tags
- Create short and long descriptions
- Generate embedding text for later vector search

### Stage 7 — Assets
- Download publicly available photos when clearly allowed
- Never download copyrighted or private images
- If no good photos → use placeholders and list them as missing dependencies
- Generate asset manifest

### Stage 8 — Confidence Score
Score from 0 to 100 based on:
- Number of independent sources
- Completeness of critical fields
- Consistency between sources
- Freshness of data
- Presence of official website or Google Business

### Stage 9 — Approval Package
Final output contains:

- Structured JSON (ready for database)
- Human-readable Markdown profile
- SEO metadata
- Embedding text
- Asset manifest
- Missing items report
- Confidence score + explanation
- Source log

