## 6. Output Format (Example Structure)

```json
{
  "pipeline_version": "1.0",
  "confidence_score": 87,
  "status": "pending_approval",
  "duplicate_candidates": [],
  "place": { ... },
  "business_details": { ... },
  "media": [],
  "seo": {
    "title_es": "",
    "title_en": "",
    "description_es": "",
    "description_en": ""
  },
  "tags": [],
  "embedding_text": "",
  "sources": [
    {
      "field": "phone",
      "value": "+52...",
      "source": "https://...",
      "confidence": "high"
    }
  ],
  "missing": [
    "opening_hours",
    "good_cover_photo"
  ],
  "notes_for_human": ""
}

7. Modular Architecture (for future strength)
The system must be built as independent modules:
textcip/
├── input_parsers/          ← TikTok, Instagram, Google Maps, etc.
├── collectors/             ← Website scraper, Google, social, etc.
├── normalizers/            ← Name, address, phone cleaning
├── duplicate_detector/
├── enrichment/             ← SEO, tags, embeddings
├── asset_handler/
├── scoring/
├── output_generators/      ← JSON, Markdown, etc.
└── orchestrator.py         ← Main workflow controller
Adding a new source later = only add a new collector + parser.
The rest of the pipeline stays the same.

8. Human Approval Interface (Future)
Simple view that shows:

Confidence score (big)
Side-by-side: Draft vs possible duplicate
Missing items highlighted
One-click: Approve / Edit / Reject
Quick edit fields for the most common fixes


